Label the angle $JKL = x$, the angle bisector of angle $J$ intersects $KL$ at point $U$, and the angle bisector of angle $K$ intersects $JL$ at point $V$. We know that the sum of all the angles in $JKL$ is $180$, so then $x+60+30 = 180$, so $x = 90$. We also know that the angle bisector divides the angle into two equal parts somehow, so $JKU = KLU = 45$ and $JKV = LKV = 15$. Because $JKU = CJM$ and $KJV = CMJ$, angle $M = 180 - 45 - 15 = (\boxed{120})$.


